1
00:00:02,600 --> 00:00:05,125
We would like to share
the development direction

2
00:00:05,178 --> 00:00:07,440
for our new JEI English
program in the U.S.

3
00:00:07,890 --> 00:00:11,400
We will also explain the curriculum
design we have developed so far.

4
00:00:13,150 --> 00:00:16,603
In the U.S., reading education
based on the Science of Reading,

5
00:00:16,657 --> 00:00:20,110
or SoR, is expanding through state
laws and education policies.

6
00:00:20,560 --> 00:00:22,946
SoR brings together scientific research on

7
00:00:23,003 --> 00:00:25,730
how children learn to read
and understand texts.

8
00:00:26,180 --> 00:00:28,801
In the U.S., this research
is being used to improve

9
00:00:28,853 --> 00:00:31,320
reading education policies
and teaching methods.

10
00:00:32,970 --> 00:00:37,905
However, according to the 2024 National
Assessment of Educational Progress,

11
00:00:37,971 --> 00:00:42,840
or NAEP, about 40% of fourth-grade
students scored Below Basic in reading.

12
00:00:43,290 --> 00:00:47,190
This shows that there is still a strong
need to improve literacy skills.

13
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:51,975
Major states, including New
York, New Jersey, California,

14
00:00:52,030 --> 00:00:55,220
Florida, and Texas, are also
introducing related policies.

15
00:00:55,670 --> 00:00:58,726
Major education companies,
such as Amplify, Lexia,

16
00:00:58,787 --> 00:01:01,660
and Savvas, also emphasize
SoR-based curricula.

17
00:01:03,310 --> 00:01:07,730
In response to these changes, we aim
to develop a new JEI English program.

18
00:01:08,180 --> 00:01:12,142
The program will help students build
skills step by step, from basic reading

19
00:01:12,194 --> 00:01:16,000
to vocabulary, reading comprehension,
and broader language understanding.

20
00:01:16,450 --> 00:01:19,320
It will also help students
develop their thinking skills.

21
00:01:20,970 --> 00:01:24,500
Our goal is to go beyond simply
reading and understanding texts.

22
00:01:24,950 --> 00:01:27,453
We want students to think
independently, make

23
00:01:27,509 --> 00:01:30,290
decisions, and express
their ideas using evidence.

24
00:01:31,940 --> 00:01:35,086
To achieve this, we plan to
build a learning system that

25
00:01:35,142 --> 00:01:38,681
connects JEI's strengths in precise
assessment and personalized

26
00:01:38,737 --> 00:01:41,770
learning plans with POD
workbooks and center coaching.

27
00:01:43,520 --> 00:01:46,600
Our target students range
from Pre-K through Grade 9.

28
00:01:47,050 --> 00:01:49,658
We have organized the
program into four levels

29
00:01:49,715 --> 00:01:52,040
based on students' stages of development.

30
00:01:53,690 --> 00:01:58,100
JEI Reading Ready is designed
for Pre-K through Grade 2.

31
00:01:58,550 --> 00:02:02,850
It focuses on building the basic skills
students need to read independently.

32
00:02:04,300 --> 00:02:07,360
Reading Builder is designed
for Grades 3 through 5.

33
00:02:07,810 --> 00:02:11,890
It helps students expand their vocabulary
and background knowledge through reading.

34
00:02:13,340 --> 00:02:16,040
Reading Plus is designed
for Grades 6 and 7.

35
00:02:16,490 --> 00:02:19,048
It helps students develop
deeper thinking skills

36
00:02:19,102 --> 00:02:21,340
by comparing and analyzing what they read.

37
00:02:22,790 --> 00:02:26,350
Finally, Reading Pro is
designed for Grades 8 and 9.

38
00:02:26,800 --> 00:02:29,248
It helps students evaluate information and

39
00:02:29,307 --> 00:02:31,930
express their ideas
logically using evidence.

40
00:02:33,580 --> 00:02:37,260
Through these four programs, we aim
to help students grow step by step.

41
00:02:37,710 --> 00:02:40,102
They will move from
basic reading skills to

42
00:02:40,157 --> 00:02:42,660
analysis, evaluation,
and building arguments.

43
00:02:44,310 --> 00:02:50,270
Overall, we plan to develop 11 levels
with a total of 352 standard sets.

44
00:02:50,720 --> 00:02:53,631
We plan to provide the
content through POD workbooks

45
00:02:53,687 --> 00:02:56,150
first and later expand
into online learning.

46
00:02:56,600 --> 00:02:59,472
However, we will continue to
review and improve the number

47
00:02:59,521 --> 00:03:02,740
of sets and learning objectives
at each level during development.

48
00:03:04,690 --> 00:03:07,660
We will now explain the key
features of the new program, what

49
00:03:07,709 --> 00:03:10,630
makes it different, and how we
are designing the curriculum.

50
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:13,500
Our new program has four main features.

51
00:03:14,950 --> 00:03:17,360
First, we focus on building reading skills

52
00:03:17,418 --> 00:03:20,000
step by step based on
the Science of Reading.

53
00:03:20,450 --> 00:03:24,340
We are designing the program to match
each student's reading development.

54
00:03:24,790 --> 00:03:28,148
Students will move from basic
reading skills to vocabulary

55
00:03:28,206 --> 00:03:30,870
and reading comprehension
in a structured way.

56
00:03:32,320 --> 00:03:36,370
Second, we provide integrated
literacy learning based on context.

57
00:03:36,820 --> 00:03:39,367
We connect different
types of texts, including

58
00:03:39,422 --> 00:03:42,190
literary and informational
texts, under one theme.

59
00:03:42,640 --> 00:03:44,962
Students will learn reading comprehension,

60
00:03:45,018 --> 00:03:47,340
vocabulary, grammar, and writing together.

61
00:03:48,790 --> 00:03:52,060
Third, we plan to provide
precise Adaptive Assessment.

62
00:03:52,510 --> 00:03:55,970
Fourth, we plan to use AI to
support learning and coaching.

63
00:03:56,420 --> 00:03:59,810
We are considering using AI for
writing feedback, POD workbook

64
00:03:59,865 --> 00:04:03,310
grading, learning result analysis,
and center coaching support.

65
00:04:04,960 --> 00:04:08,100
Next, we will explain
what makes JEI different.

66
00:04:08,550 --> 00:04:12,848
Our main goal is to connect precise
assessment, personalized learning paths,

67
00:04:12,905 --> 00:04:16,920
customized POD workbooks, and center
coaching into one learning system.

68
00:04:17,370 --> 00:04:19,926
Through this approach, we
aim to provide students

69
00:04:19,978 --> 00:04:22,430
with a unique personalized
learning experience.

70
00:04:24,080 --> 00:04:26,864
We also plan to reflect each
state's education standards

71
00:04:26,914 --> 00:04:29,350
in our learning objectives
and learning sequence.

72
00:04:29,800 --> 00:04:32,310
At the same time, we will
adjust learning content

73
00:04:32,361 --> 00:04:35,230
through Adaptive Learning
based on each student's level.

74
00:04:35,680 --> 00:04:39,450
This will allow us to provide a higher
level of personalized learning.

75
00:04:41,300 --> 00:04:43,900
Now, we will explain
our curriculum design.

76
00:04:44,350 --> 00:04:47,583
We have selected eight common
themes based on topics from

77
00:04:47,640 --> 00:04:50,760
major U.S. textbooks and
grade-level standards in CCSS.

78
00:04:52,410 --> 00:04:54,570
We use a spiral curriculum structure.

79
00:04:55,020 --> 00:04:58,890
This means students revisit the same
themes across different grades.

80
00:04:59,340 --> 00:05:02,566
As students move to higher
grades, the topics become deeper,

81
00:05:02,620 --> 00:05:05,470
and the level of reading and
thinking also increases.

82
00:05:07,120 --> 00:05:10,280
For example, let's look at the
theme of Animals and Nature.

83
00:05:10,730 --> 00:05:14,140
In Pre-K, students begin by
learning about animals around them.

84
00:05:14,590 --> 00:05:18,860
In Grade 4, they learn how animals
survive and adapt to their environments.

85
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:21,986
By Grade 9, students
evaluate and build arguments

86
00:05:22,041 --> 00:05:24,990
about their responsibility
to protect the environment.

87
00:05:26,640 --> 00:05:30,090
We have also adjusted the balance
between literary and informational

88
00:05:30,140 --> 00:05:32,880
texts based on students'
grade levels and development.

89
00:05:33,330 --> 00:05:36,820
In the early grades, we place
more focus on literary texts.

90
00:05:37,270 --> 00:05:39,820
This helps students become
more familiar with reading.

91
00:05:40,270 --> 00:05:43,361
As students move to higher
grades, we increase the amount of

92
00:05:43,413 --> 00:05:46,710
informational texts and texts
related to arguments and opinions.

93
00:05:47,560 --> 00:05:52,510
We developed these ratios as JEI's own
guidelines, using the reading standards

94
00:05:52,574 --> 00:05:57,080
in CCSS and the grade-level assessment
structure of NAEP as references.

95
00:05:58,730 --> 00:06:00,753
Through this curriculum design, we want

96
00:06:00,805 --> 00:06:03,140
students to develop more
than reading skills.

97
00:06:03,590 --> 00:06:07,350
Even within the same theme, students
will gradually build vocabulary,

98
00:06:07,404 --> 00:06:11,110
background knowledge, analysis
skills, and critical thinking skills.

99
00:06:13,060 --> 00:06:15,375
Finally, we will explain an example of our

100
00:06:15,430 --> 00:06:18,130
workbook design and our
future development plans.

101
00:06:18,580 --> 00:06:21,185
First, we will introduce
a sample Reading Builder

102
00:06:21,238 --> 00:06:23,950
workbook developed for Grade
3 students in the U.S.

103
00:06:24,400 --> 00:06:27,370
The sample uses one theme,
Building a Home Together.

104
00:06:29,020 --> 00:06:32,440
We connect literary and informational
texts under this theme.

105
00:06:32,890 --> 00:06:36,067
The learning activities move
from reading comprehension

106
00:06:36,125 --> 00:06:38,320
to analysis, application, and writing.

107
00:06:39,970 --> 00:06:43,390
We also follow JEI's
small-step learning approach.

108
00:06:43,840 --> 00:06:46,174
The weekly learning schedule includes one

109
00:06:46,231 --> 00:06:48,850
center session and four
days of home learning.

110
00:06:50,500 --> 00:06:53,130
The learning activities are
connected step by step.

111
00:06:53,580 --> 00:06:56,850
Students begin with vocabulary
preparation before reading.

112
00:06:57,300 --> 00:07:00,961
They then move to reading the
main text, reading comprehension,

113
00:07:01,019 --> 00:07:03,460
advanced vocabulary, grammar, and writing.

114
00:07:03,910 --> 00:07:07,350
This structure is designed to help
students learn independently.

115
00:07:09,000 --> 00:07:12,210
Each set includes 24 pages
of learning content.

116
00:07:12,660 --> 00:07:17,340
It also includes two pages for the
Interim Test, answer sheets, and covers.

117
00:07:17,790 --> 00:07:19,730
The total is 32 pages.

118
00:07:21,380 --> 00:07:23,930
However, this is a
standard sample workbook.

119
00:07:24,380 --> 00:07:28,090
We are currently studying how to
apply personalized POD learning.

120
00:07:28,540 --> 00:07:31,226
Our goal is to adjust and
assign the right content

121
00:07:31,280 --> 00:07:33,590
based on each student's
assessment results.

122
00:07:35,440 --> 00:07:38,150
Finally, we will explain
our next development steps.

123
00:07:38,600 --> 00:07:41,152
We have completed our
review and analysis of

124
00:07:41,210 --> 00:07:44,110
ELA education standards
across all 50 U.S. states.

125
00:07:44,560 --> 00:07:46,870
We are now working to match JEI's learning

126
00:07:46,925 --> 00:07:49,620
objectives with each state's
education standards.

127
00:07:51,070 --> 00:07:55,080
As part of this process, we are reviewing
our existing learning objectives.

128
00:07:55,530 --> 00:07:57,856
We are checking whether
they are appropriate and

129
00:07:57,904 --> 00:08:00,230
whether they follow the
right learning sequence.

130
00:08:00,680 --> 00:08:03,360
We plan to improve any
areas that need changes.

131
00:08:04,810 --> 00:08:07,575
At the same time, we are
analyzing the content

132
00:08:07,635 --> 00:08:10,580
of our existing JEI English
workbooks in the U.S.

133
00:08:11,030 --> 00:08:14,600
We are reviewing which content
can be used in the new program.

134
00:08:15,050 --> 00:08:17,735
Based on these findings, we
will connect the improved

135
00:08:17,786 --> 00:08:20,370
learning objectives with
state education standards.

136
00:08:20,820 --> 00:08:23,507
We will then develop a
more detailed theme-based

137
00:08:23,563 --> 00:08:25,970
curriculum and personalized
learning paths.

138
00:08:27,420 --> 00:08:32,040
Next, we plan to use AI Agents to develop
content for each learning objective.

139
00:08:32,490 --> 00:08:35,440
Our researchers will review
and improve the content.

140
00:08:35,890 --> 00:08:39,430
We will then build a content pool
and use it for product development.

141
00:08:41,080 --> 00:08:43,598
Rather than developing
all four programs at the

142
00:08:43,651 --> 00:08:46,490
same time, we plan to focus
on Reading Builder first.

143
00:08:46,940 --> 00:08:49,955
We will conduct a pilot test
to check learning results

144
00:08:50,011 --> 00:08:52,580
and how well the program
works at JEI centers.

145
00:08:53,030 --> 00:08:57,410
After this, we plan to expand development
to the other programs step by step.

146
00:08:59,160 --> 00:08:59,740
Thank you.

